<title>PHILIPPINES: Petron maintains lead in oil market.</title>
<headline>Petron maintains lead in oil market.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine oil refiner Petron Corp has cornered the biggest market share at 41.7 percent of the Philippine oil market for the first seven months of the year, industry figures showed.</p>
<p>Pilipinas Shell Petroleum Corp, a unit of Royal Dutch Shell Group, has 33.8 percent while Caltex (Philippines) Inc, a joint venture between US-based Chevron Corp and Texaco Inc, has the lowest share at 24.5 percent.</p>
<p>The total oil inland market of the three refiners amounted to 75.42 million barrels for the first seven months of the year, a 5.0 percent rise from last year's 71.85 million barrels.</p>
